# The two axial forms for equal opposite-side normals

The direct form is an actual half-turn whose center is forced to the square's
center by horizontal symmetry of a compact nonempty two-piece union.  The
reversing form has an explicit inverse, squares to a vertical translation,
and is conjugated to its inverse by horizontal reflection.
